# Files excluded from the build context of web/Dockerfile ([DOCKER-003],
# [DOCKER-006]). Everything listed here is either reproduced inside the image by
# the build itself, irrelevant to it, or must never enter it.

# Installed inside the builder from package-lock.json; a host copy would be the
# wrong platform and would defeat the cached install layer.
node_modules

# Build artefacts of a host-side `next build`. The image builds its own; copying
# a stale .next in is how a container ends up serving yesterday's bundle.
.next
out
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Test suite and its harness - run by `make -C web test`, not by the image.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
vitest.config.ts
vitest.setup.ts

# Local environment files. A real .env would bake developer-machine values (and
# secrets) into an image layer; .env.example is documentation and the build
# takes its one build-time value from --build-arg instead.
.env
.env.*

# Documentation and editor/VCS metadata.
*.md
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Tooling that plays no part in `next build`.
Makefile
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.prettierrc
